+    // NOT a reliable "did the active map's pose origin just change" signal:
+    // clearMap() (used by Tracking::ResetActiveMap(), the path actually
+    // taken by both the "Not enough motion for initializing" and "IMU is
+    // not or recently initialized" resets seen in live testing) clears and
+    // re-initializes the SAME Map object in place, so its mnId never
+    // changes, even though every point/keyframe was just discarded and
+    // tracking restarts from a fresh origin. This counter changes on every
+    // reset that can affect the pose origin, regardless of which path.
+    long unsigned int GetResetGeneration();
